			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>Guest Mode lets someone look at a few photos on your iPhone without the rest of your library, or the rest of your iPhone, within reach.

1. In Photos, tap the round Guest Mode button and choose up to 10 photos or videos. The button turns blue and shows how many.
2. Tap the button again. After Face ID, Photos shows only what you chose: a small gallery to swipe through, zoom and play. There is nothing else to scroll to, and nothing to share, edit or delete.
3. Tap the button (now a lock) once more. After Face ID, Photos is back to normal and the selection is forgotten.

Hold the button to change or clear the selection. Drag it to move it.

Guest Mode stays on when Photos is closed and opened again.</string>
		</dict>
