			<string>enabled</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Guest Mode Button</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>Stay in Photos switches off the Home gesture, the App Switcher, Control Centre, Notification Centre, Siri, screenshots and the double click for Wallet, and brings Photos straight back if anything else gets in front. Only Face ID on the Guest Mode button ends it.

Held notifications make no sound and show nowhere; they all arrive when Guest Mode ends. A declined call lands in Recents as a missed call.

The side button still locks the iPhone; unlocking it leads back to the same photos. Emergency SOS keeps working. Should Photos itself fail while Guest Mode is on, the iPhone locks its screen and lets go, so you are never shut out of it.</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>While Guest Mode Is On</string>
